Hi Bob,

> I=92m a new guy to linux on the alpha=85

Welcome!

> Just got an AS 4100 server and was looking for a distro of linux to =20=

> put on it. Has anyone on the list had any luck with this machine and =20=

> Debian?


The only supported binary distribution for Alpha is the Debian Lenny =20
release and it is now getting a bit old.   The Alpha architecture is =20
not included in the newer Debian Squeeze release (the aim is to =20
release early February).

Debian still has Alpha in its unstable development and in some regards =20=

is better than Lenny (a number of important bugs are fixed) but is =20
worse in others (there are some new very annoying bugs and the X =20
window server only runs on BWX capable Alphas).  I'm not sure whether =20=

the AS4100 comes with BWX capable CPUs (maybe someone else can comment =20=

on that) but if it does then I recommend you install Lenny (as the =20
unstable distribution has no Alpha installer) then upgrade to =20
Unstable.  If you want a web browser to work on it you will need to =20
compile your own one as the Debian supplied iceweasel, etc., is broken =20=

on Alpha.

I am currently running Debian Unstable on an XP1000 and PWS600au.  =20
Much of it is working well but some desktop programs (web browsers, =20
thunderbird, etc.) crash too regularly to be useful.  In contrast =20
OpenOffice works well!

Also feel free to join #alpha on IRC.

Cheers
Michael.



